{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"completion_prefetch_manifest":[{"mode":"full","path":"referencing-commit ca89152f7b3ff02178352de3db13a3fad9a56fbc"}],"criteria":[{"citation":{"description":"RCA comment (ticket timestamp 1788648085610426001): hypothesis stated as nginx 60s proxy_read_timeout vs legitimate packfile silent gaps; disproof condition: if Gerrit/httpd returned failures or if slow requests did not align with nginx 504s at the edge. Ticket description checkbox [x] with inline evidence pointer.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"AC1 A falsifiable hypothesis for the 504s is stated, with the observation that would disprove it, BEFORE any fix.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"RCA comment (timestamp 1788648085610426001): 4 incident fetches mapped to Gerrit HTTP 200 responses lasting 85-94s while nginx logged 504 at 60s; proxy config confirmed missing directive; CPUCreditBalance hit 0.0 at 12:38 UTC 2026-09-05; IO hypothesis explicitly refuted (Gerrit git data on separate EBS nvme1n1, not root filesystem).","kind":"source"},"criterion":"AC2 The mechanism is established by correlating 504 timestamps against host-side evidence (Gerrit/httpd logs, proxy timeout configuration, host IO and CPU at those instants) — not by plausibility. The IO hypothesis above must be confirmed or refuted explicitly.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"RCA comment (timestamp 1788648085610426001) explicitly distinguishes: (1) proxy timeout too short for legitimate packfile work — raising it is a fix; (2) host cannot serve in reasonable time — separate capacity finding with different remedy (credits/instance-class/tenancy).","kind":"source"},"criterion":"AC3 If the cause is a proxy/gateway timeout that is simply too short for legitimate packfile work, say so — raising it is then a fix, not a workaround. If instead the host cannot serve in reasonable time, that is a capacity finding and needs a different remedy. Distinguish them.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Ticket 7c9b-3afe-5a6f-4254 confirmed to exist with alias 'imprudent-national-monkey', status 'open', with a `discovered_from` link (link_uuid f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8) pointing to 5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1. Ticket description states 'This was AC4 of antihuman-beefwitted-zebra (5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1).'","kind":"source"},"criterion":"AC4 Split out to `imprudent-national-monkey` (7c9b-3afe-5a6f-4254), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Ticket comment (timestamp 1788747581555724001): before-rate 4/40 (10%) Gerrit Verified Gate runs failing in checkout with 504 signature, host-side 12/37 (32.4%) CI fetches over 60s ceiling, replicated 2/6 (33%). After 2026-09-06T01:05:39Z nginx reload: 14 runs, 12 non-cancelled, 12 successes, 0/12 = 0.0% post-fix.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"AC5 A measurable before/after rate is recorded, using the PARTITIONED counts above rather than the raw 55%.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Gerrit location / block now has proxy_read_timeout 600s (line 200), replacing the implicit 60s default. Deployed to live host per ticket comments with final_count=4 confirmed. Post-fix rate 0/12 = 0.0% checkout transport failures.","kind":"file","line_end":201,"line_start":183,"path":"infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template"},"criterion":"Bug 'Gerrit returns HTTP 504 on git fetch, breaking CI checkouts across sessions' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_basis":"unpinned_completion_inputs","material_fingerprint":"38c8e23cc6447f9f","